  "summary": "Nihon Hidankyo, the Japan Confederation of A- and H-Bomb Sufferers Organizations, was founded on 10 August 1956 in Nagasaki by survivors of the Hiroshima and Nagasaki bombings. It campaigns for the welfare of survivors and for abolition of nuclear weapons, and received the 2024 Nobel Peace Prize.",
